  "live_records": {
    "q-101158": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101158",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate ${lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{{t}^{2}+t-6}{{t}^{2}-9t+14}.$",
      "worked_solution": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{{t}^{2}+t-6}{{t}^{2}-9t+14} & =\\frac{{2}^{2}+2-6}{{2}^{2}-9(2)+14}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{t}^{2}+t-6}{{t}^{2}-9t+14} & =\\frac{(t+3)(t-2)}{(t-2)(t-7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{t+3}{t-7}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{{t}^{2}+t-6}{{t}^{2}-9t+14} & ={lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{t+3}{t-7} \\\\  & =\\frac{2+3}{2-7} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{(-5)} \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
