</mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle><mjx-tstrut></mjx-tstrut></mjx-mtd></mjx-mtr></mjx-itable></mjx-table></mjx-mtable></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"block\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"block\"><mtable rowspacing=\".5em\" columnspacing=\"0.278em\" displaystyle=\"true\" columnalign=\"right left\"><mtr><mtd><munder><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OP\" movablelimits=\"true\">lim</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"ORD\"><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></munder><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>12</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>64</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>64</mn></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>0</mn><mn>0</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>So, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. </p>\n<p>Notice that the denominator is a sum of cubes. Therefore, factoring our expression, we get</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"16\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 14.987em;\"><mjx-table