    "q-338206": {
      "dom_id": "step-q338206",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{7{y}^{6}-3{y}^{4}}{5{y}^{5}+10{y}^{4}}=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{7{y}^{6}-3{y}^{4}}{5{y}^{5}+10{y}^{4}} & =\\frac{7(0)^{6}-3(0)^{4}}{5(0)^{5}+10(0)^{4}}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, to find the limit, we have to factor the numerator and the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7{y}^{6}-3{y}^{4}}{5{y}^{5}+10{y}^{4}} & =\\frac{{y}^{4}(7{y}^{2}-3)}{{y}^{4}(5y+10)} \\\\  & =\\frac{7{y}^{2}-3}{5y+10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{7{y}^{6}-3{y}^{4}}{5{y}^{5}+10{y}^{4}} & ={lim}_{y\\to 0}\\frac{7{y}^{2}-3}{5y+10} \\\\  & =\\frac{7(0)-3}{5(0)+10} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
